1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,349
Why can't you tickle yourself?

2
00:00:02,389 --> 00:00:03,813
Same fingers, same spot,

3
00:00:03,853 --> 00:00:05,377
and nothing happens.

4
00:00:05,417 --> 00:00:06,441
Your brain is one step

5
00:00:06,481 --> 00:00:07,792
ahead of you.

6
00:00:07,832 --> 00:00:09,056
Every time you move,

7
00:00:09,096 --> 00:00:10,120
it keeps a copy

8
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:10,971
of the command

9
00:00:11,011 --> 00:00:12,247
and predicts exactly

10
00:00:12,287 --> 00:00:14,024
what you're about to feel.

11
00:00:14,064 --> 00:00:15,300
Your cerebellum sends

12
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:16,777
that prediction ahead,

13
00:00:16,817 --> 00:00:18,266
and the touch is turned down

14
00:00:18,306 --> 00:00:19,830
before it arrives.

15
00:00:19,870 --> 00:00:21,107
Scientists in London

16
00:00:21,147 --> 00:00:22,883
tested it with robots.

17
00:00:22,923 --> 00:00:23,947
When people moved

18
00:00:23,987 --> 00:00:24,798
one robot arm

19
00:00:24,838 --> 00:00:26,500
and another touched their palm

20
00:00:26,540 --> 00:00:27,764
at the same moment,

21
00:00:27,804 --> 00:00:29,328
it hardly tickled.

22
00:00:29,368 --> 00:00:30,179
Add a delay

23
00:00:30,219 --> 00:00:31,869
of a fifth of a second,

24
00:00:31,909 --> 00:00:33,645
and the tickle came back.

25
00:00:33,685 --> 00:00:34,922
Your brain only lets you

26
00:00:34,962 --> 00:00:35,773
feel a tickle

27
00:00:35,813 --> 00:00:37,762
when it can't see it coming.

28
00:00:37,802 --> 00:00:39,039
Subscribe for more strange facts

29
00:00:39,079 --> 00:00:40,743
about your body.
